  "verbalization": "Marsdekoiside A appears to have a direct target relationship with Hepatocyte through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Marsdekoiside A acts as a target for Carboxylesterase 2, which in turn is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound, in turn, targets Hepatocyte, indicating a potential pathway where Marsdekoiside A influences Hepatocyte function via a downstream enzyme cascade. The shared target of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One across multiple paths suggests a common mechanism of action, possibly involving the modulation of metabolic pathways in liver cells. The integration of these relationships highlights a possible role for Marsdekoiside A in modulating hepatic function through the activation or inhibition of key enzymes, with Hepatocyte being the ultimate cellular target.",
